226:The example below builds one tool per warehouse table. A map return names each tool by its bare key, so the model sees `orders`, `users`, and so on.
312:A dynamic connection, tool, or skill whose name matches an **authored** one **overrides** it — a per-caller resolver can replace a static capability by name. Two **dynamic** resolvers of the same capability type emitting the same name is a genuine ambiguity and throws; namespace one of the keys manually to resolve it.
318:| `session.started` | At session start; may be redelivered during recovery¹ | Every model call in the session |
319:| `turn.started`    | Once per turn                                         | Every model call in the turn    |
320:| `step.started`    | Before each model call                                | That model call                 |
332:The tool loop reads the current set right before each model call, so a mid-turn update is visible on the next call.
334:A single file can declare handlers for several events, and the most recently fired one owns that file's tool set. Re-resolve on `turn.started` to replace what `session.started` returned:
