     1	---
     2	title: "Built-in Tools"
     3	description: "The default and opt-in tools eve provides, including glob, grep, and sleep."
     4	---
     5	
     6	eve provides a default tool set for every agent and additional tools you can add with one file. Each default occupies the same `agent/tools/<name>.ts` slot you would author yourself, so an authored definition replaces it and `disableTool()` removes it. Use this page to review what the model can call, opt into more capabilities, or override and disable defaults. For custom tools, see [Tools](../tools).
     7	
     8	## Default tools
     9	
    10	Default tools require no imports. The exact set depends on the agent and session, and the harness advertises only the tools available to the current session.
    11	
    12	### Disable optional default tools
    13	
    14	Optional default tools are enabled unless you set `defaultTools: false` in `agent/agent.ts`:
    15	
    16	```ts title="agent/agent.ts"
    17	import { defineAgent } from "eve";
    18	
    19	export default defineAgent({
    20	  defaultTools: false,
    21	  model: "openai/gpt-5.4",
    22	});
    23	```
    24	
    25	This turns off the optional defaults described below. Add back only the tools the agent needs with the command in each tool's section. Existing files under `agent/tools/` remain available, including same-name replacements such as `agent/tools/bash.ts`.
    26	
    27	`connection_search` stays available when the agent has connections because it provides access to their tools.
    28	
    29	### `bash`
    30	
    31	`bash` runs shell commands in the agent's [sandbox](../sandbox).
    32	
    33	```sh
    34	eve add tool/bash
    35	```
    36	
    37	```ts title="agent/tools/bash.ts"
    38	export { default } from "eve/tools/bash";
    39	```
    40	
    41	Override its description, approval policy, or executor by wrapping the exported definition:
    42	
    43	```ts title="agent/tools/bash.ts"
    44	import { defineTool } from "eve/tools";
    45	import { bash } from "eve/tools/bash";
    46	
    47	export default defineTool({
    48	  ...bash,
    49	  description: "Run approved project maintenance commands.",
    50	  async execute(input, ctx) {
    51	    console.info("Running sandbox command", input.command);
    52	    return bash.execute(input, ctx);
    53	  },
    54	});
    55	```
    56	
    57	Disable only `bash`:
    58	
    59	```ts title="agent/tools/bash.ts"
    60	import { disableTool } from "eve/tools";
    61	
    62	export default disableTool();
    63	```
    64	
    65	### `read_file`
    66	
    67	`read_file` reads text files from the sandbox with line-numbered output. It accepts absolute paths and paths beginning with `$HOME/`.
    68	
    69	```sh
    70	eve add tool/read_file
    71	```
    72	
    73	```ts title="agent/tools/read_file.ts"
    74	export { default } from "eve/tools/read_file";
    75	```
    76	
    77	Override it:
    78	
    79	```ts title="agent/tools/read_file.ts"
    80	import { defineTool } from "eve/tools";
    81	import { readFile } from "eve/tools/read_file";
    82	
    83	export default defineTool({
    84	  ...readFile,
    85	  description: "Read project files from the sandbox.",
    86	});
    87	```
    88	
    89	Disable it:
    90	
    91	```ts title="agent/tools/read_file.ts"
    92	import { disableTool } from "eve/tools";
    93	
    94	export default disableTool();
    95	```
