codex
The first-turn wait checks whether a bot or model selection exists, not whether the required instruction blocks rendered successfully. I also found a migration hazard: `updateShell()` calls `readShell()` while holding the lock, so adding a locking migration inside `readShell()` needs a separate internal read path. I’m finishing the checks for legacy history, prompt size and dropped round-1 safeguards.

